      "title": "Possible replacement patch over 'INR 98,700' in salary_slip",
      "severity": "medium",
      "confidence": 0.8,
      "status": "potential_manipulation",
      "explanation": "The PDF draws a bordered rectangle (fill #f5f2e8, border #d4cfbf) on top of the panel behind 'INR 98,700'; the panel is #e0edf2, so the rectangle stands out in colour as well as by its border. The figure on it is set in Courier, a different font family from the 7 other amounts on the page (helvetica). A bordered patch with different lettering is a common way to cover a printed number and write another one. This is an observation about how the file was built: it does not show that the value was changed, by whom or why, and a design element can look similar. Compare with the issuer's original.",
